{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-splade-llama70b", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Cold water can actually be beneficial for recovery, especially when it comes to reducing pain and inflammation. When you apply cold water to an injured area, it constricts the blood vessels, which can help reduce swelling and ease pain. This is because cold water slows down the flow of blood to the area, which can help reduce the amount of fluid that accumulates in the tissues. Additionally, cold water can help reduce muscle spasms and stiffness, making it easier to move the affected area. However, it's essential to note that cold water should not be used for an extended period, as it can cause tissue damage. It's recommended to apply cold water for 15-20 minutes, several times a day, to help promote recovery. It's also crucial to consult with a medical professional before using cold water therapy, especially if you have any underlying medical conditions. They can provide personalized advice and guidance on how to use cold water therapy safely and effectively.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0010-90-05991:13": 4.920249938964844, "clueweb22-en0010-90-05991:12": 3.7217397689819336, "clueweb22-en0029-54-15395:15": 3.215068817138672, "clueweb22-en0040-78-04000:12": 3.070863962173462, "clueweb22-en0010-90-05991:11": 2.6613609790802}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "Many years ago I had a bad fall while bouldering."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0010-90-05991:13": 4.920249938964844, "clueweb22-en0010-90-05991:12": 3.7217397689819336, "clueweb22-en0029-54-15395:15": 3.215068817138672, "clueweb22-en0040-78-04000:12": 3.070863962173462, "clueweb22-en0010-90-05991:11": 2.6613609790802, "clueweb22-en0017-96-08323:5": 2.583155632019043, "clueweb22-en0042-02-14356:5": 2.434133768081665, "clueweb22-en0032-15-04383:2": 2.353806495666504, "clueweb22-en0001-63-00419:2": 2.2633447647094727, "clue