{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-splade-llama70b", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The National Health and Medical Research Council (NHMRC) is Australia's peak body for supporting health and medical research, developing health advice for the Australian community, health professionals, and governments, and providing advice on ethical behavior in healthcare and in the conduct of health and medical research. It aims to raise the standard of individual and public health in Australia and foster the development of consistent health standards between the various states and territories. The NHMRC brings together within a single national organization the functions of research funding and development of advice, drawing upon the resources of all components of the health system. Its mission is to build a healthy Australia. The NHMRC has a statutory responsibility to engage in activities to achieve its intentions and foster the consideration of ethical issues relating to health. It achieves its functions through various activities, including issuing and approving clinical practice, public health, and environmental guidelines, developing standards and advice for guideline developers, maintaining the Australian Clinical Practice Guidelines Portal and Register, and funding health and medical research.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0003-28-18244:1": 6.409040451049805, "clueweb22-en0021-65-00357:0": 6.38991641998291, "clueweb22-en0036-34-08990:0": 5.579414367675781, "clueweb22-en0013-50-10617:6": 5.567690372467041, "clueweb22-en0021-15-14465:0": 5.408954620361328}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0003-28-18244:1": 6.409040451049805, "clueweb22-en0021-65-00357:0": 6.38991641998291, "clueweb22-en0036-34-08990:0": 5.579414367675781, "clueweb22-en0013-50-10617:6": 5.567690372467041, "clueweb22-en0021-15-14465:0": 5.408954620361328, "clueweb22-en0030-66-12544:0": 5.127133369445801, "clueweb22-en0034